# AI Docs
AIDOCS/
### Interior Bazzar — no JSON in the repo
# Matches the backend rule: every .json is ignored project-wide. Already-tracked files
# (package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig*.json, src/locales/*/translation.json)
# stay tracked — git ignores untracked files only — but any NEW json, a new locale file
# included, has to be forced in with `git add -f` or it will silently never be committed.
*.json

# ...except the mock-API content, which is SOURCE, not config or build output.
# src/content/<module>/*.json stands in for endpoints that do not exist yet (see
# src/proto/v-2.2.0.0/BACKEND-INTEGRATION.md). Those files are the only thing
# some screens render from — ignored, the module builds and shows nothing for
# anyone who clones. The blanket rule above was silently swallowing the whole
# directory, and `git add -f` every time is a rule somebody forgets once.
!src/content/**/*.json
